> Extract out the logic into a common helper void VisitSymbol(ISymbol symbol, Action<Diagnostic> reportDiagnostic, Location location, SymbolDisplayFormat format)

I wanted to avoid creating a delegate per operation/symbol (`reportDiagnostic`). There's ways around it but dey nasty. 

```C#
        private void VisitSymbol<TContext>(TContext context, Compilation compilation, Action<TContext, Location> reportDiagnostic, ISymbol symbol, Location location)
        {
            if (symbol.ContainingAssembly == compilation.Assembly)
            {
                // This is part of the compilation, avoid this analyzer when building from source.
                return;
            }

            if (HasInternalAttribute(symbol))
            {
                reportDiagnostic(context, location);
                return;
            }

            var containingType = symbol.ContainingType;
            if (IsInInternalNamespace(containingType) || HasInternalAttribute(containingType))
            {
                reportDiagnostic(context, location);
                return;
            }
        }
```

I think I'd prefer the code duplication.
